    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a clear focal point in **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (82.13), who headlines our lineup. His elite sprint speed aligns perfectly against J. Irvin\u2019s slow delivery, and with a favorable +14% boost from a dynamic platoon advantage and a leadoff spot, he is the highest-ceiling asset on the board. We are also leaning heavily into the matchup against Carson Whisenhunt, where **Yordan Alvarez** (76.93) and **Nelson Velazquez** (66.15) benefit from both a struggling southpaw and wind blowing out, helping **Yordan Alvarez** overcome his inherent platoon disadvantage to provide elite production. **Junior Caminero** (77.68) remains an anchor in the heart of the order, capitalizing on a hitter-friendly park environment against Mason Barnett.\n\nThe most difficult decision for the optimizer involved **Carson Benge** (50.14), who narrowly missed the starting cut. While **Carson Benge** presents a decent baseline, his score was suppressed by a poor platoon matchup against M. P\u00e9rez, leaving him just behind the established floor of the primary nine. We are also monitoring a 33% rain risk in the game featuring **Chase Meidroth** (57.36); while he remains in the lineup due to his projected volume, his utility is secondary to the high-efficiency potential of **Trea Turner** (65.12), whose speed profile makes him a critical engine for our stolen base targets against Andre Pallante. We continue to bench **Jacob Gonzalez** (39.13) as he fails to meet our 40-point efficiency threshold, opting to prioritize the higher-upside profiles of our active starters to protect our game caps.",
